  "body": "Session closeout for the thingalog-vars-canonicalization arc. Opened by PO 'could you check for memos' which surfaced two new inbound memos from thingalog-strategist (2026-06-03-2130 and 2026-06-03-2330) — the substrate-touching-variable routing channel established by the 2026-05-27T2216 thingalog-ux-engineer CC memo had fired with its first concrete ask. **What was drafted (with paths):** (1) [decisions/CA-018.md](../decisions/CA-018.md) — three-call disposition: catalog-vs-application framing adopted as catdef-canonical guidance (Call 1); .x-subtitle → canonical .subtitle on Catalog root with root-only inheritance (Call 2); .x-quick_filters → items in .views reserved subcat with View template (label/filter/sort), root-only inheritance, subcat shape chosen over flat var (Call 3); 3 chrome vars (.x-header_style + .x-card_meta_fields + .x-card_footer_field) confirmed permanent .x- per the framing; §2.2 Presets+Views unification withdrawal concurred; filter grammar deferred to its own cycle. Four build directives: maintainer proposal artifacts (Directive 1); conformance tests (Directive 2); framing addendum to CONTRIBUTING.md or CLAUDE.md (Directive 3); v1.5 activation surfaced for Director (Directive 4 — recommends Path A bundled v1.5 over Path B incremental v1.4.x minor). (2) [memos/2026-06-04-1000--catdef-strategist--thingalog-strategist--acceptance-of-narrowed-canonicalization-ask-ca-018.openthing](2026-06-04-1000--catdef-strategist--thingalog-strategist--acceptance-of-narrowed-canonicalization-ask-ca-018.openthing) — cross-spec acceptance memo closing the loop on the 2-of-5 ask; informational; CA-018 is the formal authority. (3) This closeout. **What was decided:** CA-018 — the substantive strategist call. Subordinate design calls captured within: subcat-over-flat-for-quick_filters (five-reason justification — .presets precedent + native structure + future-proofing + MCP parity + operational-metadata-as-reserved-subcats doctrine); filter opaque-string-for-now (defers filter grammar work); translatable .subtitle (per v1.4 polymorphic-translatable-field pattern); root-only inheritance for both new fields (matches Thingalog's _NON_INHERITED_ABOUT_KEYS precedent). **What's in flight (started but didn't land):** (a) Plugin remains under Anthropic review ('Submitted and pending review' as of last check; no review-decision memo yet); milestone memo filed when status changes. (b) catdef-maintainer queue now carries four bundled items: CA-013 Call 3 (canonical-implementor identity acknowledgment) + CA-015 Directive 1 (security doctrine in CLAUDE.md or SECURITY.md) + CA-016 Directive 2 (renderer/ row in repo-table; CONTRIBUTING + CLAUDE.md mentions) + CA-018 Directives 1+2+3 (.subtitle and .views proposal artifacts + conformance tests + framing addendum). No urgency increase; all bundle into next maintainer session. (c) canonical-implementor v0.2 backlog unchanged (feedback_audit table, mechanical catdef_validate, Durable Object for CA-NNN, resourceTemplates exposure, self-serve key issuance). (d) v1.5 cycle remains Director-triggered; CA-018 is the empirical activator surfaced for that trigger. **What's open (surfaced but not addressed):** (a) CA-014 + CA-017 in MCP queue at triaged-for-v0.2; D1↔MCP column mapping for CA-014 fix concrete (from prior session). (b) CA-015 negative-space amendment (don't grep ~/.claude.json for bearer) — flagged in prior session; not yet filed. (c) refresh-counter behavior verification (max vs overwrite) — still owed; canonical-implementor task. (d) Filter grammar codification — CA-018 explicitly defers; CLAUDE.md §Known Work Items flags as natural next deliverable; awaits its own cycle. (e) Future thingalog substrate-touching variable asks — channel works end-to-end now; expect more arrivals over time. (f) generative-lens thread — thingalog-strategist's primary; this seat holds the through-line for any substrate-touching aspects. **Notable observations worth carrying forward in seat history:** (1) The substrate-touching-variable routing channel established by the 2026-05-27T2216 thingalog-ux-engineer CC memo has now produced its first concrete strategist disposition. End-to-end validation: thingalog-ux-engineer flagged routing pattern → thingalog-strategist did design thinking + bundled ask + refinement → catdef-strategist disposed via CA-018 → maintainer drafts proposals → Director ratifies → spec text merges in v1.5 (or v1.4.x if Path B). Pattern works as designed. (2) The catalog-vs-application framing PO ratified on the thingalog side is sharp enough to apply retrospectively to all future .x- vars without re-deriving each time. CA-018 Call 1 formalized it as catdef-canonical guidance. The cut: 'is the concept renderer-portable?' Yes → canonical; No → permanent .x-. This pre-positions future strategist sessions for consistent calls. (3) Subcat shape over flat var for operational metadata is the established pattern (.presets precedent + now .views per CA-018 Call 3). Future operational metadata candidates default to subcat shape unless flat-var-only is clearly indicated. (4) The CA-NNN collision pattern that materialized 2026-05-26 was preempted this session via proactive counter bump (UPDATE meta SET value = '18' WHERE key = 'ca_nnn_counter'). Lesson from prior session applied: when filing a strategist-initiated decision that doesn't have a paired feedback item, bump the counter immediately post-commit to prevent the next feedback submission collision. (5) CA-010 reference-user demand bar applied cleanly to CA-018 — Thingalog's empirical demand across multiple production catalogs (welch-arctic-collection chrome work, magazine-flow catalog cards, AI-curator-as-quick-filter-author Saved Views) satisfied value #4 without needing a second non-Thingalog implementer. Channel + CA-010 + standard pipeline produced a coherent disposition. **What future incumbents of this seat should know:** (i) The substrate-touching-variable channel is operational; future thingalog asks land in catdef-spec/memos/ addressed to catdef-strategist; disposition via CA-NNN; CA-010 makes the demand bar straightforward. (ii) The catalog-vs-application framing (CA-018 Call 1) is the established test for promotion calls; check renderer-portability before deciding. (iii) Subcat shape over flat var for operational metadata is the established pattern; .presets + .views are precedents; flat var only when the data has no internal structure. (iv) Counter-bump after strategist-initiated CA-NNN commits is the established pattern; UPDATE meta SET value WHERE key = 'ca_nnn_counter' via wrangler (PO holds D1 auth). (v) v1.5 cycle remains queued; CA-018 is now its empirical activator; Director's trigger gate is unchanged. (vi) Plugin review is still pending at claude-community marketplace; status memo when review-decision arrives. (vii) Five closeouts now in this seat's chain (2026-05-26-1100, 2026-05-26-1900, 2026-05-29-1730, and this 2026-06-11); read the chain on fresh onboard.",
